{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:66813395d2adf3ce","name":"PTV-2100 Incarcerator","source":{"id":"source:reference-66813395d2adf3ce","title":"PTV-2100 Incarcerator","revision":21232,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:24:12Z","sha256":"d54e77e6a0b091f25d74922c6e66ad01fa78c497c2ce6bf416d9c080e25d6a06","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21232","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=PTV-2100%20Incarcerator&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-66813395d2adf3ce","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy of Intrigue"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_of_Intrigue"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Designed by Kuat Drive Yards during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", the PTV-2100 is a lucrative, if understated, transport vessel. The sole purpose of this vessel is the transport of prisoners, including some of the most dangerous individuals in the galaxy. Heavily armed, the Incarcerator is a slow and ponderous Starship, so it relies on smaller, more nimble ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," for protection. Although used primarily by governments, Incarcerators are also employed by large criminal organizations for hauling individuals to the spice mines or slaves to markets in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Outer Rim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Outer_Rim?action=edit&redlink=1"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The greatest part of an Incarcerator is devoted to prison cells of various size and security, including minimum-security holding pens and thick-walled, heavily shielded isolation rooms with redundant protective measures. The hallways and cells are outfitted with cameras and sensors to monitor the inmates, and guard stations feature weaponry to quell riots or to stun or kill escapees.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The PTV-2100 Incarcerator is a slow, ponderous vessel, so other ships can easily catch up with it. However, it excels at repelling boarding actions. The Incarcerator and all allies in adjacent squares gain an additional die of damage against ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," moving into the same square as the Incarcerator to dock with it or board it.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["PTV-2100 Incarcerator Statistics (CL 16)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal (Frigate) ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -4; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 13 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 13), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 40; +13 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Combat","referenceId":"reference:31246426131b3457"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 1,600; ",{"tag":"a","children":[